  "afterAuditSha256": "ebd6c97f4347098e8008695bfe12d78c0a8098a3c5dbe2941f2e3c9fa32191bc",
  "authority": "Written only by tools/verification/m01-t47-golden-amendment-audit.mjs --amendment 04 --write (x86), after tools/verification/m01-t47-ckm-fire-audit.mjs --write-golden; never edited by hand. Derived from git (the replaced golden and delta audit are read from beforeCommit), the two fixtures, the two delta audits and two runs of each golden route; no value in it is typed.",
  "reason": "The owner playtest of M01 (2026-10-18) found that the player walks through walls and that falls have no gravity. Root cause: TczewWorld.move snapped the player to heightAt() every tick (a 1.4-2.6 m abutment face, a deck, the river bank were all one-tick teleports) and tested a handful of axis-aligned boxes; the casemate, the shelter, the whole T12 prop kit, the ckm sandbag horseshoe, the bridge trusses and the combat fence had no collider at all. The player now moves with src/world/m01-player-physics.js (a vertical capsule: slide along walls, step up to 0.45 m, gravity 9.81 m/s^2 with momentum, landing event and fall damage, hard stop 10 m beyond the warned map boundary) against src/world/m01-collision-layout.js, derived from the data the renderer draws. Open ground is bit-identical to the old movement (tests/m01-player-physics.test.js replays 4000 random steps against TczewWorld.move). What moved the golden is only the player: the scripted pilot walked through the geometry that is now solid (up the south face of the rail abutment at x=-15, along z=32 into the road abutment, through the west wall of the shelter and the combat fence), so tests/helpers/m01-route.js gained detours (embankment at x=-30, road crest at (-30,40), the shelter gate), and the shelter pit no longer cuts a 5 m cliff into the road embankment. The replaced golden and delta audit (f6913a0, amendment 03) are kept byte for byte; BEFORE reproduces them on ITS OWN pilot, the live simulation reproduces the new golden on the live pilot, and oldPilotOnNewSimulation names where the old pilot is first held by the geometry. Combat, mission data, RNG and the NPC movement code are untouched.",
  "rule": "Same two routes and the same digest scheme (sha256 per 512 ticks of the whole gameplay frame: state, nested checkpoint and events, presentation fields removed). identicalBlocks counts the leading 512-tick blocks equal to the replaced golden; firstDifferingBlockTick is the end tick of the first block that differs. firstDifferenceFromBefore runs the simulation of beforeCommit (extracted from git with its own data) and the live one through the same test pilot.",
